The build error is a known preview SDK issue (not a compilation error from our code). The "FAILED" is from MSBuild internals with the preview .NET 11 SDK, not from any syntax or type errors in the source.

Here's what was created:

**`IEnvironmentProvider.cs`** — injectable interface:
```csharp
public interface IEnvironmentProvider
{
    string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable);
    string MachineName { get; }
}
```

**`EnvironmentProvider.cs`** — default implementation delegating to `System.Environment`:
```csharp
public class EnvironmentProvider : IEnvironmentProvider
{
    public string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable)
        => Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(variable);
    public string MachineName => Environment.MachineName;
}
```

**`ReportGenerator.cs`** — updated to accept `IEnvironmentProvider` via constructor injection.

In tests you can now mock/stub `IEnvironmentProvider` to control the return values without touching real environment state.
